  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Gavi, the Vaccine Alliance 
Dutch contribution to Gavi 6.0 (2026 - 2030), core contribution and Matching Fund.</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">GAVI, officially Gavi, the Vaccine Alliance is a public&#x2013;private global health partnership with the goal of increasing access to immunization in poor countries. It was founded in 2000 and is located in Geneva. 
Gavi is active in 54 countries, both in humanitarian and developing contexts.

Since its inception, Gavi has helped immunize over 1 billion children, preventing over 20.6 million deaths thus far. The Netherlands has helped save the lives of 645,298 children with 37,756,782 vaccines delivered between 2000 and 2020.

Gavi is an innovative and effective partnership that works closely with the WHO, UNICEF, the World Bank, the vaccine industry and implementing countries.</narrative>
  </description>
